      "mergeID": "62916d336d67c01e5526bddd",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I am currently using an Oculus Quest 2. I use owoTrack as my hiptracker, and I use two HTC Vive Wands as feet trackers. After the IK update, the Vive Wands no longer work during FBT Calibration. When calibrating in game, my hip (owoTrack) calibrates fine, but my Vive Wands are ignored (even though I can see the white balls on my feet). After in game calibration, my hip is the only thing that works, and my feet trackers do not work.\nI really hope this can be fixed, because I have been using this hybrid FBT for a few days while also using the IK beta, and it worked. I've been absolutely loving it, and I'd hate to see it completely gone from the game.\nIn case this helps, I use OpenVr SpaceCalibrator to get the Vive Wands to match up with my Quest 2.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Vive Wands no longer work as trackers",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "629088ad6d967c0b63c5d1f8",
